diff --git a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/socket-api.mdx b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/socket-api.mdx
index 547415a..74d28a8 100644
--- a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/socket-api.mdx
+++ b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/socket-api.mdx
@@ -17,6 +17,18 @@ Most automation should start with the CLI wrappers. Use the raw socket API only
 
 The layers share the same control surface.
 
+For OpenCode V2, `agent.prompt` does not type into the terminal. Its visible TUI
+frontend polls the server's `agent.delivery.poll` method with `pane_id` and the
+selected root `root_id`, then confirms the returned `delivery_id` through
+`agent.delivery.complete` after admitting the message via OpenCode's
+`session.prompt({ sessionID: root_id, text })`. The first registered root is
+fixed for that agent process: browsing another root cannot redirect delivery;
+returning to the original root resumes it. Child routes keep their root.
+An unavailable frontend, root mismatch, or unconfirmed delivery fails explicitly
+without replaying the text as terminal input. A timeout after dispatch has an
+uncertain outcome: inspect the session before retrying manually. Other agents
+retain their existing terminal submission behavior.
+
 ## Schema
 
